<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21025] quota: slave doesn't reintegrate after LWP reconnects to restarted master</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21025</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When an MDT (the quota master) restarts, the LWP on each OST/MDT slave&lt;br/&gt;
reconnects to it and goes through "lwp recover" (&lt;tt&gt;ptlrpc_connect_interpret()&lt;/tt&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;OBD_CONNECT_LIGHTWEIGHT&lt;/tt&gt;). &lt;tt&gt;lwp_import_event()&lt;/tt&gt; then cancels the global quota&lt;br/&gt;
locks locally on &lt;tt&gt;IMP_EVENT_INVALIDATE&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;qsd_glb_blocking_ast()&lt;/tt&gt; doesn't restart reintegration for local cancels&lt;br/&gt;
(&lt;tt&gt;LDLM_FL_LOCAL_ONLY&lt;/tt&gt;), because it treats them as stack cleanup or eviction.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;qsd_conn_callback()&lt;/tt&gt; is only called on the first connect. So nothing restarts&lt;br/&gt;
reintegration: the slave's global and slave index copies stay out of date&lt;br/&gt;
until the writeback thread notices and retries. In testing that took ~115&lt;br/&gt;
seconds after the master restart.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During that window the slave misses limits set on the master. An ID that&lt;br/&gt;
wasn't enforced before isn't enforced on the OSTs, and its writes don't&lt;br/&gt;
acquire quota from the master, so users can exceed new hard limits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer: sanity-quota &lt;tt&gt;test_7c&lt;/tt&gt; (restart mds during reintegration). The test&lt;br/&gt;
passes, but the OSTs need ~120s (&lt;tt&gt;wait_ost_reint&lt;/tt&gt;) to reintegrate after the MDT &lt;br/&gt;
restart. The debug log shows "lwp recover", then "losing global index lock"&lt;br/&gt;
for each type, then no "Starting reintegration thread" until the writeback&lt;br/&gt;
thread retries ~115s later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Measured (single-node VM, 1 MDT + 2 OSTs, master 2.17.60, 10 runs of&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;test_7c&lt;/tt&gt; each):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class='table-wrap'&gt;
&lt;table class='confluenceTable'&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;without patch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;with patch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;total time of 10 runs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;1377s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;371s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;&lt;tt&gt;test_7c&lt;/tt&gt; time, median (min-max)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;140.5s (108-143)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;24s (23-142)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;OST reintegration wait after MDT restart, median&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;120s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;5s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The single 142s run with the patch hit a separate race (see ticket 2). That&lt;br/&gt;
race exists without this patch as well.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: restart reintegration on a local cancel of the global lock if the import&lt;br/&gt;
is still valid (not on qsd/LWP cleanup or eviction), and make the &lt;br/&gt;
reintegration thread wait for the import to be FULL before enqueueing the &lt;br/&gt;
global lock.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
